    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a challenging slate today, highlighted by several high-end starters like Skubal and Misiorowski, which suppresses our overall ceiling. Our strongest play is **Kyle Tucker** (51.97), whose pedigree and high base projection allow him to maintain a solid efficiency score despite the daunting matchup against Dodd. Close behind is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (51.04), benefiting from a significant +14% dynamic platoon boost against the right-handed Rasmussen, and **Jackson Merrill** (50.99), who carries the most offensive momentum despite the elite 2.35 xERA of Misiorowski. These three remain our anchors as we prioritize high-floor producers to maintain our 5x5 Roto standing.\n\nThe primary bench decision centered on **Brayan Rocchio** (34.60), who fell well below our 40.00 floor threshold. While he typically offers utility, his placement in the 9th spot of the order and a negative SP skill adjustment against Smith stripped away his viability for today's rotation. With **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** off today and **Jordan Westburg** remaining sidelined on the IL, our depth is thinner than usual, necessitating a cautious approach to conserve game caps. We are effectively punting the bottom of our bench to ensure that our starters\u2014particularly **Liam Hicks** (40.84) and **Andy Pages** (44.23)\u2014are protected from further negative variance. Owners should monitor the lineup status for **Miguel Vargas** (47.23) and **Drake Baldwin** (47.11); while both are currently slated for starts, their scores are sensitive to any late-game defensive substitutions or pinch-hit threats given the quality of the opposing arms.",
